## If something goes wrong

| What you see | What to do |
|---|---|
| `Wrong password or the file was changed` | The password does not match this file, or the file was edited. Password mode does not use the port. |
| `already exists` / output exists | Pick another output path, move the old file, or pass overwrite (`overwrite=True`, `{ overwrite: true }`, `overwrite: true`, the Java `true` flag). |
| `File not found` | Seal from the file’s real path. Open the `.Red_SecretXAI` you just wrote, not the original. |
| JavaScript, C#, Java, or C++ refuses a PNG | That SDK reads binary containers in 0.3.1. [Convert the PNG back](Red-X-PNG.md) to `.Red_SecretXAI`, then open it. Python `decrypt_file` reads the PNG form directly. |

The command line’s `encrypt-file` uses a [port](Port-mode.md), not this password-mode API. For a self-contained file, use the SDK calls on this page.

